Execution: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent execution lifecycle, action model, and tool
  abstraction.

ExecutionLifecycle:
  REQUESTED:
    ?
  PLANNED:
    ?
  AUTHORIZED:
    ?
  EXECUTING:
    ?
  VERIFIED:
    ?
  COMPLETED

Failure:
  EXECUTING:
    ?
  FAILED:
    ?
  ROLLBACK / RECOVERY

ActionModel:
  ACTION:
    ModifyFile

  Target:
    ./<layer>/<domain>/<module>/<artifact>

  Reason:
    <task-id>

  Risk:
    <R0-R5>

  Policy:
    ALLOWED

  Verification:
    go test ./...

AgentRun:
  RUN-YYYYMMDD-NNN

  Structure:
    INPUT
    CONTEXT
    PLAN
    ACTIONS
    VERIFICATION
    RESULT
    AUDIT

Tools:
  DockerTool:
    BUILD, RUN, COMPOSE, EXEC, CP
    rule: ALL tool execution MUST go through DockerTool
    rule: no direct shell execution outside Docker
  FileTool:
    READ, SEARCH, CREATE, UPDATE, MOVE, DELETE
    rule: file operations inside Docker volumes only
  GitTool:
    STATUS, DIFF, LOG, BRANCH, CHECKOUT, COMMIT, MERGE, TAG
    rule: git operations inside Docker container
  TestTool:
    UNIT, INTEGRATION, E2E, BDD
    rule: tests run inside Docker container with resource limits
  DatabaseTool:
    MIGRATE, SEED, QUERY
    rule: database operations inside Docker container only

ToolRules:
  [EX1]  Agent MUST use tool abstraction, not hard-code operations.
  [EX2]  Shell commands MUST be allowlisted.
  [EX3]  Agent MUST NOT push to production by default.
  [EX4]  Agent MUST verify after each action.

State: +
